# Screens: a tool or gun pulled out of the inventory into the hand. With the laser on one in your own inventory, the grip
# squeezed and the hand drawn back toward you (15 cm) puts it in the hand through the game's own switch to that item.
# World: Earth Planet (survival, on foot). A pistol is given so the inventory surely holds a gun; the hand starts empty.
# The plugin says where the item is on the panel once the inventory page is shown, as in screens-inventory-toolbar.vrtest.

plugin SpaceEngineersVR
world game:Earth Planet

# ---- What the world needs: a gun in the inventory ----------------------------------------------------------------------

give PhysicalGunObject/SemiAutoPistolItem
log SpaceEngineersVR.log
expect session focused within 60

head 0 1.6 0
hand left -0.25 1.0 -0.3
hand right 0.25 1.0 -0.3 0 -60
wait 1
# Before: nothing in the hand.
read character
expect weapon == null
key I
wait 2
read screens
expect result contains MyGuiScreenTerminal

remember tool log '/Inventory toolbar: on the panel, .* the first tool or gun you carry, (\S+), at stage/' within 10
remember toolAt log '/Inventory toolbar: on the panel, .* the first tool or gun you carry, \S+, at stage \((\S+), (\S+), (\S+)\) m/' within 10

# ---- A grip let go before the pull takes nothing -------------------------------------------------------------------------

hand right 0.1 1.55 -0.2 toward {toolAt}
wait 1
expect log Laser: pointing at the panel within 5
press right grip
wait 0.5
expect log /Inventory pull: Right grip on the .* in the inventory/ within 5
release right grip
wait 0.5
expect log Inventory pull: let go of the within 5
read character
expect weapon == null

# ---- The grip, then the hand drawn back 25 cm: it comes into the hand -------------------------------------------------------

press right grip
wait 0.5
hand right 0.1 1.55 -0.1 toward {toolAt}
wait 0.3
hand right 0.1 1.55 0.05 toward {toolAt}
wait 1
expect log came out of the inventory into the Right hand within 5
# The grip was the pull's, never the right mouse button.
expect no log Laser: right button down
release right grip
wait 0.5
read character
expect weapon.item contains {tool} within 5
expect no log Exception

key Escape
wait 1
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenGamePlay
